                "fills": [
                  {
                    "fillColor": "#9ea3b0",
                    "fillOpacity": 1
                  }
                ],
                "fontFamily": "Inter",
                "text": "Touching the strip opens the Loop panel over the whole readout (layout B, owner decision 2026-11-04). The header keeps the track, its state and length, and a small live waveform, so the player still sees the loop while editing; Done (accent, 88\u00d748) closes it, and so do 10 s without a touch. Left, the tempo card: the tempo in hundredths in JetBrains Mono 44 with the beat lights (the downbeat ringed amber, the current beat accent), a dotted rule that marks the figure as the way into exact entry (08), then -1, -0.1, +0.1, +1 (hold to repeat; decision 3) and Clear tempo beside Tap. Tap is outlined in accent and acts on touch-down rather than release, so the tap lands where the hand did; Clear tempo was added after build 229 (owner, 2026-11-05) and goes through the same engine lock as the main screen's. Right: the time signature (3\/4, 4\/4, 6\/8 and More for all 17, 07), the length of the next take (-, value, +, Auto; 1 to 64 bars) and Start, the record timing's seven values. Length and Start edit the all-tracks default (decision 2). The selected value takes accentSurface with a 1 px accent edge. Every control is at least 48 logical high (77 physical), and the sections share one 11 px caps label style. Commands go over the screen link to TempoSettings, RecordSettings and RecordTimingSettings; the panel draws what the next push reports, not what it sent."
              }
            ],
            "textTransform": "none",
            "textAlign": "left",
            "fontId": "custom-55ea1d0f-da97-4707-a8aa-51a6f1855ee9",
